    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "Sudden electrical discharges manifested by a flash of light (lightning) and a sharp rumbling sound. Thunderstorms are associated with convective clouds (Cumulonimbus) and are more often accompanied by precipitation such as rain, hail or snow. They are usually shortlived and hit on only a small area.",
